    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "Both functions are implemented in `app/network.py`. `pytest -q` passes (3 tests), and I ran a separate check with a stub transport that confirmed every requirement.\n\n**`configure_hub_http(transport=None)`** registers a client factory with huggingface_hub (`set_client_factory`). All `HfApi` instances then share one client through `get_session()`. The client:\n- sets the header `X-Acme-Job: nightly-sync`. huggingface_hub still adds its own headers to each request, and in the check its user agent (`hf_hub/2.0.0; ...`) was still sent.\n- keeps huggingface_hub's own request hook, which handles offline mode and request IDs, and follows redirects as the library's default client does.\n- uses `transport` when one is passed.\n- applies a connect timeout of 5 seconds and read, write and pool timeouts of 60 seconds.\n\n**One catch with the timeouts:** methods like `HfApi.model_info` pass `timeout=None` explicitly by default. httpx2 (the HTTP library huggingface_hub 2.0 uses) reads that as \"no timeout\" and ignores the client's setting. So setting a timeout on the client alone does nothing for these calls. I added a small request hook that sets the 5/60-second timeouts on every request. As a result, a timeout passed to a single call is also replaced by these values.\n\n**`current_revision(repo_id)`** returns `HfApi().model_info(repo_id, revision=\"main\").sha`. It asks for `main` explicitly because the repo's default branch might not be `main`. If the connection fails or times out, it logs a warning on `app.network` and returns `None`. Any other error still raises; in the check, a missing repo raised `RepositoryNotFoundError`.\n\n**Limitations:**\n- huggingface_hub's async client is never shared (the library creates a new one each time), so this setup doesn't cover it.\n- The timeout hook relies on `hf_request_event_hook`, which is imported from the private module `huggingface_hub.utils._http`. It could move if the pinned version is ever upgraded.\n\n**Cleanup:** I wasn't allowed to delete my t"
